{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/47938-help-sidereal-swordsman-the-trouble-with-melee","id":47938,"title":"Help - Sidereal Swordsman (the trouble with Melee)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Sidereal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-12T22:38:01-08:00","id":47938,"title":"Help - Sidereal Swordsman (the trouble with Melee)","content":"I like Sidereal Melee - Jedi Charms, protective mentor, Fate-O-Vision, it's all pretty cool. So I was pondering a new character, a star-sworn knight - Sidereal swordsman. I was considering which Martial Arts Styles would go well to supplement such a concept, and found the combination of Violet Bier of Sorrows and Sidereal Melee to be pretty fun...<br /> <br /> Then I realized it wasn't possible. The errata made it so you didn't have to buy combos or spent Willpower to activate them, but the limits on combos remain - you cannot activate Charms of different Abilities as part of the same combo. This limits severely the compatibility of any MA Style with Melee, and as cool as Melee is, it has all of seven Charms.<br /> <br /> So I'm turning to the forums for help in how to design a character who can progress in combat skill past the basic Sidereal Melee Charm-set. I <i>want </i>to use Melee, so &quot;just use MAs&quot; is not the kind of answer I am looking for - rather what to spend my xp on once I'm past that stage. Some measure of Resistance Charms seems a given, but other than that, I'm not sure. <i>Are </i>there MA Styles that could work well in combination with it despite the combo restrictions(perhaps through heavy use of scene-long boosts)? Or should I turn my attention somewhere I haven't looked?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T00:50:37-08:00","id":47997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/47938-help-sidereal-swordsman-the-trouble-with-melee#post47938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then I realized it wasn't possible. The errata made it so you didn't have to buy combos or spent Willpower to activate them, but the limits on combos remain - you cannot activate Charms of different Abilities as part of the same combo.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not <i>entirely</i> true. Look for the words &quot;must&quot; and &quot;may&quot; in the Timing guidelines for Combos (on page 245). &quot;Must&quot; is compulsory, &quot;may&quot; is optional. Also check the charms themselves for exceptions.<br /> <br /> For instance, Supplemental charms <i>must</i> benefit the Simple charm of the combo if there is one, or non-reflexive actions if there is not. This normally requires them to be of the same Ability, but not always (refer to <i>Meditation on War</i> for a Supplemental Melee charm that explicitly may combo with other Ability attack charms and supplement them).<br /> <br /> On the other hand, Supplemental charms <i>may</i> benefit Reflexive action, if it's valid to do so (this <i>normally</i> requires them to be of the same Ability, unless indicated otherwise). Thus Reflexive charms and Supplemental charms of different Abilities can be included in the same Combo, the Reflexive action just does not benefit from the Supplemental charm.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T01:34:53-08:00","id":48012,"title":"","content":"You are being very confusing, mr Greyman. It's far simpler than that - and not entirely as you write.<br /> 1) The ability restriction you mentioned is a Supplemental Charm thing(supp charms by default only enhance the ability they're in), rather than a combo thing.<br /> 2) On Combos:<br /> Simple Charms: can only have one, and have to use it. If there's an extra action, you have to use the Simple on all extra actions.<br /> Supplemental Charms: As many as you want. You have to use all Supplementals on all actions contained in the combo.<br /> Extra Action charms: like Simple: can only have one, and have to use it.<br /> Reflexive Charms: no restrictions, use at your leisure.<br /> Charms have to have the Combo-Ok or Combo-Basic keyword to be used in a combo. The former is thoughtless. The latter may only combo with reflexive charms. IIRC Form-Type also means Combo-Basic.<br /> 3) On top of it all you have overdrive: Charms entirely paid with overdrive do not count as charm use, and do not interact with combos at all, so you can use them pretty much freely.<br /> ----------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> Consider Throne Shadow Form + Meditation on War. Every time one of your Fingers Parries you gain 2m. Sure, this restricts your ability to use other Forms, but if you're fighting with a significant group your overdrive just went on super crack, and you can use it on them. And later there's always Prismatic Arrangements of Creation Form.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":32,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","user":"Synapse","date":". 01-13-2014, 05:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T02:24:39-08:00","id":48022,"title":"","content":"I played a sidereal swordsman before, and this setup worked well enough. Make sure to pick up World-Shaping Artistic Vision with something like &quot;Swords&quot; as your category, so that you can subtract your stunt value from the target number of every attack. Once you get Perfection of the Visionary Warrior you'll be able to attack multiple times at low cost, while ignoring both action and onslaught penalties. Use heavy armor combined with the scene long medicine charm for absurd soak, and pick up Shield of Fate from resistance to remove ping while also returning the damage to the attacker. If you use a starmetal Grand Daiklaive you will get decent damage, and with World-Shaping Artistic Vision and Fateful Melee Excellency you will also hit just about anything. Impeding the Flow combined with Blinding the Boar should give you decent DV.<br /> <br /> This worked nicely in the early parts of the campaign, but if you plan on playing this character for a long time you will eventually run into trouble with the closed charm set. Sidereals not having any melee charms above essence 4 will make you fall behind at high xp. When I ran into this issue, I picked up Monkey Style. It works with all armor and weapons once you master it, and it has a few charms that are really good. The DV charm is ridiculously overpowered, and being able to throw an attack before combat even begins is quite nice. You can't combo the charms with melee, but they still have some uses.<br /> <br /> Basically, sidereal melee works decently on low levels, but you'll regret it if you choose to use this charm set in either a really long campaign or if the other players are combat optimized solars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1935-paradigm","name":"Paradigm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T02:48:54-08:00","id":48030,"title":"","content":"Simplest solution, use your Melee charms for defense and use VBoS for attacking. Come to think of it, this is also every splat's solution to MA styles having awful defensive charms. Or just make some attacks with MA and others with Melee and use charms accordingly. I mean, it's not like you're combining multiple charms onto the same attack roll that often.<br /> <br /> edit: So I just looked over the Sidereal Melee charm set and the only two charms that you would have trouble with are Orchestration of Mirrored Fates, a counter-attack charm, and Smiling At The Damned, a charm for adding stacking a little extra ping on the target. Considering the nature of these charms I'd say not being able to stack MA supplementals on top of these isn't a big problem. Harmony of Blows and Perfection Of The Visionary Warrior allow you to make Martial Arts attacks so no problems there and the other three are overdrive or defense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":407,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/407-ithle","user":"Ithle","date":". 01-13-2014, 06:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/407-ithle","name":"Ithle","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T04:03:57-08:00","id":48056,"title":"","content":"Alright, well first, VBoS only fails to function with Flight of Mercury, Life-Severing Blow, and Metal Storm. The rest work with Melee, although the Form isn't as useful if you're not doing MA. And on the flip side, as Ithle said, only Orchestration of Mirrored Fates and Smiling at the Damned doesn't work with MA. <br /> <br /> As always I suggest talking to your ST about custom Charms. VBoS Style isn't stretching thematic boundaries very much, and Sidereal Melee is fairly straightforward -- you could probably replicate a good amount of VBoSS in Sidereal Melee straight-up, then continue to make straightforward custom Melee Charms from there. Or you could could make upgrades to Orchestration of Mirrored Fates and Smiling at the Damned to allow them to work with non-Melee Abilities; that wouldn't be out-of-theme for Sidereal Melee, seeing how some of them do allow for that already.<br /> <br /> There are also other useful combat Charms scattered around the Sidereal set. Not only Resistance, but Athletics and Awareness as well, along with Craft, Dodge, Integrity, and Performance (depending how far you want to spread yourself).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11I0xCPgAS3ZhxGvTlBoePOuaDqgpyWs13jVKhJ4c8hM/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Book of the Emerald Circle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/37100-white-elephant-for-flintlock-sidereal-custom-charms-and-discussion-on-themes\" target=\"_blank\">Custom Sidereal Charms</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sQxyi3ox0qn53c_vsUaVQi_pRdpKlQE50NT5ldQmxYI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Expanded Sidereal Linguistics</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/263-limited-reagent","name":"Limited Reagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar263_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T09:30:52-08:00","id":48235,"title":"","content":"Hm. Only three Charms that can't be combo'd in MA, plus Blade of the Battlemaiden being redundant due to you already having a starmetal sword, is still just under half the style. On the other hand, the only two Melee Charms that don't work with MA combos aren't my favorite anyway, so.... It might just work.<br /> <br /> I'd overestimated the importance of the combo thing, it seems. Cool. Now I'm left with regret that VBoS doesn't allow armor, and that the only style I can remember allowing both armor and (short) swords is Fire Dragon. That's annoying; I wanted to be a knight in starmetal armor. <br /> <br /> So I'm down to either unarmored VBoS/Melee sword-fighting, or asking for custom Charms and spreading competency far and wide to get combat Charms from other abilities. All right. I always try to pick up WSAV, anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T09:44:40-08:00","id":48248,"title":"","content":"Silken Armor and Discreet Essence Armor will do the trick until you get that stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T09:45:02-08:00","id":48249,"title":"","content":"How optimized a game are we talking about? I'm pretty sure you can have a lot of fun with just Melee Charms and artifact gear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T10:23:04-08:00","id":48291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/47938-help-sidereal-swordsman-the-trouble-with-melee?p=48235#post48235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd overestimated the importance of the combo thing, it seems. Cool. Now I'm left with regret that VBoS doesn't allow armor, and that the only style I can remember allowing both armor and (short) swords is Fire Dragon.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Technically</i> there's also Five Dragon Style. <i>Technically.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T11:02:23-08:00","id":48321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/47938-help-sidereal-swordsman-the-trouble-with-melee?p=48248#post48248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Silken Armor and Discreet Essence Armor will do the trick until you get that stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Surely you mean &quot;or&quot;. And I disagree.<br /> <br /> ****<br /> <br /> How hung up are you on the sword? And how do you feel about Celestial Monkey or Silver Voiced Nightingale?<br /> <br /> I forget... isn't Snake Style ridiculously permissive?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 01-13-2014, 02:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T11:08:32-08:00","id":48326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/47938-help-sidereal-swordsman-the-trouble-with-melee?p=48249#post48249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How optimized a game are we talking about? I'm pretty sure you can have a lot of fun with just Melee Charms and artifact gear.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, probably. I won't know how optimized a game this is until other people start submitting their own sheets, but I tend to go for Dex 5, Ability 5, Specialty +2/+3 in all circumstances anyway; beyond that... I don't know! I do want superheavy plate. Not for &quot;maximum soak&quot; but for the aesthetics of the knight in full plate armor (which, granted, I could do with mundane armor). With a huge sword. Which basically restricts me to Melee. <br /> <br /> Maybe I should just not sweat it and go with Melee then broaden my focus to other Abilities when I run out. But it's haaaard. I'll probably end up making custom Charms and picking up stuff in... Resistance/Craft/Integrity, say.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T12:01:15-08:00","id":48376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/47938-help-sidereal-swordsman-the-trouble-with-melee?p=48326#post48326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, probably. I won't know how optimized a game this is until other people start submitting their own sheets, but I tend to go for Dex 5, Ability 5, Specialty +2/+3 in all circumstances anyway; beyond that... I don't know! I do want superheavy plate. Not for &quot;maximum soak&quot; but for the aesthetics of the knight in full plate armor (which, granted, I could do with mundane armor). With a huge sword. Which basically restricts me to Melee.<br /> <br /> Maybe I should just not sweat it and go with Melee then broaden my focus to other Abilities when I run out. But it's haaaard. I'll probably end up making custom Charms and picking up stuff in... Resistance/Craft/Integrity, say.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dex 5 is de rigeur for Exalted, but honestly? Skip trying to optimize beyond it and let the character grow organically. Sure, you waste a lot more XP than your pre-optimized counterparts, but then your character doesn't become wrapped up in absolutely having to be a brilliant swordsman.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T12:19:41-08:00","id":48389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How hung up are you on the sword? And how do you feel about Celestial Monkey or Silver Voiced Nightingale?<br /> <br /> I forget... isn't Snake Style ridiculously permissive? </div> </div> </div>Snake Style is &quot;hook swords and seven-section staves.&quot; Celestial Monkey requires low Virtues, which doesn't square with (Virtue) Essence Replenishment, and which I personally don't find fun (I like crazy-high Virtues); Silver Voiced Nightingale would be a completely different character. I am trying to go for a &quot;medieval knight&quot; look, though I could spare the armor for the sake of VBoS or another style like it. <br /> <br /> Well, thanks, everyone. I got some neat advice and will give it thought.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T12:52:40-08:00","id":48416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/47938-help-sidereal-swordsman-the-trouble-with-melee?p=48326#post48326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, probably. I won't know how optimized a game this is until other people start submitting their own sheets, but I tend to go for Dex 5, Ability 5, Specialty +2/+3 in all circumstances anyway; beyond that... I don't know! I do want superheavy plate. Not for &quot;maximum soak&quot; but for the aesthetics of the knight in full plate armor (which, granted, I could do with mundane armor). With a huge sword. Which basically restricts me to Melee.<br /> <br /> Maybe I should just not sweat it and go with Melee then broaden my focus to other Abilities when I run out. But it's haaaard. I'll probably end up making custom Charms and picking up stuff in... Resistance/Craft/Integrity, say.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, you're probably not going to start with all Melee Charms anyway, and artifact sword and armor will give you some leeway in 2.5 (unlike in 2.0 where armor was a hindrance and any sword other than Grand Daiklave was mostly window dressing). You can probably keep yourself busy buying just native Sid Charms until at least the 200 exp mark, and unless the campaign is crazy high powered, you should stay relevant all the time (Melee is essential to Sidereal builds anyway).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T13:04:03-08:00","id":48424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/47938-help-sidereal-swordsman-the-trouble-with-melee?p=48326#post48326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, probably. I won't know how optimized a game this is until other people start submitting their own sheets</div> </div> </div> </div>This situation seems remarkably familiar...<br /> <br /> \u200bSpeaking from a purely hypothetical position, I agree with Dayen and Morangais. It would likely be best to start with a handful of Melee charms and see where you evolve the character from there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T21:08:57-08:00","id":48705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/47938-help-sidereal-swordsman-the-trouble-with-melee?p=48416#post48416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, you're probably not going to start with all Melee Charms anyway, and artifact sword and armor will give you some leeway in 2.5 (unlike in 2.0 where armor was a hindrance and any sword other than Grand Daiklave was mostly window dressing). You can probably keep yourself busy buying just native Sid Charms until at least the 200 exp mark, and unless the campaign is crazy high powered, you should stay relevant all the time (Melee is essential to Sidereal builds anyway).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd have to say that all you really need is melee and archery backup for combat and you'll be set for a while. True it's not as evocative as MA as a whole but it's solid and more than able than keeping up with other Splats. Sidereal Melee is nice if nothing else than for it's ability to synergize with every other combat ability.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-14T01:28:34-08:00","id":48798,"title":"","content":"Slightly off the beaten track for your stated concept, OP, but have you looked at Holden's Wind-Cutting Blade Style? I don't have the PDF I made of it anymore, but I got really good mileage out of that every time I used it, with the exception of my Kimbery Infernal...no melee charms, no synergy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/339-armstrong-thunderbolt","name":"Armstrong Thunderbolt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar339_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-14T10:44:00-08:00","id":49116,"title":"","content":"[cracks knuckles, flexes neck] ...Let's do this.<br /> <br /> Omicron, I'm a little unclear on your campaign needs. Your PC will be hanging with other Exalted PCs, sure, but is he on his own? The Fivescore Fellowship usually expects their agents have more secrecy than tromping about in full Starmetal armor, so consider going with the Ronin option. Or he could always be on Sabbatical...Also, I'm assuming you're using the Sidereal errata because, why wouldn't you?^_^<br /> <br /> So, let's talk Caste. I'm leaning towards Battles, whose power will help Soak-wise if you decide to ditch the armor for MA reasons. Otherwise, Endings is good for the extra damage.<br /> <br /> If you're going for a master swordfighter, then you'll want to get your College of the Spear up as high as possible, to get the best use of your Excellencies. I suggest Fateful Dodge Excellency, to complement Propitious Melee Alignment, since you can't use both Excellencies with the same Ability...<br /> <br /> You can be as straight-up badass a swordsman as you want, but remember, Siddies get ahead by gaming the system, so let's talk Astrology. Slap yourself with an Ascending Destiny revolving around winning duels, probably with a Hound-Chases-Rabbit blessing that gives you a WP for every successful Ability roll relating to that.<br /> <br /> If you want to interact with folks in Creation, you'll need a Resplendent Destiny, probably from the House of Battles. I recommend the Spear, as the Someone's Son Style Resplendency power sounds like it'll fit your PC concept well. The Shield and the Banner may also fit, and the Shield has some of the best combat Resplendencies, esp the Soak one, if you go without armor.<br /> <br /> What's a knight without his trusty steed? Find a warhorse from the corebook, choose it for your Familiar, and upgrade him to a God Horse, asap. You'll have a badass mount tricked out with Spirit Charms that will put Tornado and Silver to shame (maybe not Maximus, tho)! Ride Charms are cool, but don't forget about the Messenger Resplendencies...<br /> <br /> Are you a lone knight errant, or are you forming a knightly order? If the latter, there are tons of tricks to buff up your Followers/Henchmen, which gets even scarier with Throne Shadow Style!<br /> <br /> Onto Charms. In addition to what's already been suggested, Optismistic Security Practice and Unwavering Well Being Meditation will be useful in surviving combat, and if you think you may encounter any ghosts or shadowlands, definitely invest in Medicine (do Abyssals count as Creatures of Death for Smooth Transition? If so, ouch!); Mending Warped Designs is useful for healing yourself and others from OOF attacks. You'll surely want at least one of the &quot;danger sense&quot; Awareness Charms, and in the odd event you meet a superior swordsman, use Sidereal Shell Games to steal his mojo and use his own moves against him! Auspicious Prospects for Battles will let you know which duels to accept and which to avoid, as can Wise Choice, and Force Decision can help you end situations without violence. Faultless Ceremony is really good if you have an organization, but there's nothing saying you can't perform a solo ritual (to, say, a god of dueling or Mars herself) and gain its benefits for yourself. You will clearly want to have a Destiny Knitting Entanglement on your precious sword, in case you get disarmed in combat or lose it some other way. Speaking of swords, are you committed to a daiklave? If you go the (relatively) subtle route, Blade of the Battle Maiden lets you use anything from a rusted antique to a wooden practice sword as tho they were Starmetal Daiklaves! Which leads us to sword-based MA...<br /> <br /> Five Dragon Style allows armor, as does Even Blade (tho only up to medium). Path of the Arbiter allows armor that has a value less than your MA rating, and it must have your crest on it, which suits a knight. Also, the style enables you to choose your Form Weapon, and manifest a glowing artifact version of it (also, you can summon the Armor of Integrity, and a cool mount, which should work with your Spirit Familiar)! Some people scoff at TMA for Celestials, but they're flavorful and can be taught to your minions.<br /> <br /> Silver Voiced Nightingale and Quicksilver Hand of Dreams allow swords and armor, so long as you make them according to the styles' themes. Scarlet Patterned Battlefield Style has some VERY useful combat charms, although it doesn't allow arms or armor. Of course, that could be your PCs chance to say, &quot;You think me harmless, since you've stripped me of my weapons and armor? You fool...you've just made me more dangerous than ever!&quot;<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> HTH! And don't worry, if any of the above is wrong, Epimetheus will be along shortly to point it out!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":681,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","user":"Hand-of-Omega","date":". 01-14-2014, 01:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-14T11:34:07-08:00","id":49164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/47938-help-sidereal-swordsman-the-trouble-with-melee?p=48389#post48389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Snake Style is &quot;hook swords and seven-section staves.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't like the idea of hook swords and armour? You're mixing melee and martial arts after all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Celestial Monkey requires low Virtues, which doesn't square </div> </div> </div>Fair enough.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Silver Voiced Nightingale would be a completely different character. I am trying to go for a &quot;medieval knight&quot; look </div> </div> </div>Wouldn't you say Iron Siaka fits the medieval knight aesthetic? Aside from fighting with a mace, she pretty much fits the <b>Knight</b>ingale look I was going for. But it's your character.<br /> <br /> If you want armour but not the sword you can still pull off the knight theme. Plenty of knights fight with maces. I can't tempt you with a spear/lance?<br /> <br /> Good luck on your character Omicron, sounds like a cool concept.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-14T11:51:30-08:00","id":49173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/47938-help-sidereal-swordsman-the-trouble-with-melee?p=49164#post49164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wouldn't you say Iron Siaka fits the medieval knight aesthetic? Aside from fighting with a mace, she pretty much fits the <b>Knight</b>ingale look I was going for. But it's your character.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whomever gave Iron Siaka the Nightingale Style in 2e wasn't having his best day, because it fits like a giraffe in space shuttle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-14T20:02:25-08:00","id":49493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/47938-help-sidereal-swordsman-the-trouble-with-melee?p=49116#post49116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">stuff</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh. Seems like a decent list but as a sidereal swordsmen I'd try not using MA until you absolutely have to it ruins the theme. Also an number of the non-2.5 stuff like the SMA has legitimate issues that need to be resolved before putting them into a 2.5 game..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-14T20:53:39-08:00","id":49522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/47938-help-sidereal-swordsman-the-trouble-with-melee?p=49173#post49173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whomever gave Iron Siaka the Nightingale Style in 2e wasn't having his best day, because it fits like a giraffe in space shuttle.</div> </div> </div> </div>She must be quite.........loud in the bedroom.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}